# .dockerignore — keep the build context minimal AND keep Layer B out of the
# image entirely. Anything matched here is never sent to the Docker daemon,
# so it can neither slow the build nor leak into a layer.

# --- Build artifacts (rebuilt inside the builder stage) --------------------
target/
**/target/

# --- VCS / CI metadata -----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# --- Layer B: private, runtime-only material — NEVER ship in the image -----
# Sourced at runtime from FAMILYCLAW_PROFILE_DIR / FAMILYCLAW_DATA_DIR.
.env
.env.*
profiles/
data/
hearth/
keys/
*.soul
*.soul.md
SOUL.md
**/SOUL.md
*.calibration.json
calibration.json
**/calibration.json
*.pem

# --- Docs, plans, research (not needed to build the binary) ----------------
# NOTE: do NOT blanket-exclude "*.md". Several crates embed their own README
# at COMPILE time via `#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`
# (familyclaw-bus, -agent, -dream, -memory). Excluding those READMEs would
# break `cargo build`. We exclude only top-level docs and known root-level
# markdown that are NOT compile inputs, and keep crate-local README.md files.
docs/
plans/
research/
papers.txt
research_data.md
research_plan.md
# Root-level planning / narrative markdown (not build inputs):
/BLUEPRINT.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/FAMILYCLAW_FINAL_PLAN.md
/FAMILYCLAW_MASTER_PLAN.md
/GOVERNANCE.md
/HUIPPUTUOTE_SUUNNITELMA.md
/KEHITYSSUUNNITELMA.md
/SECURITY.md
/PAKETTI-*.md

# --- Layer B / internal-only dirs + files (never enter the build context) --
# (docs/ above already excludes docs/source-blueprints, docs/plans, docs/handoff)
agentit/
ops/
core/
FAMILYCLAW_MAP.md
*SUUNNITELMA*.md
recv.py
bridge.py
write_papers.py

# --- Test fixtures / test trees (not needed for the release build) ---------
tests/
**/tests/fixtures/

# --- Local editor / OS cruft -----------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
*.log
.DS_Store

# --- The Docker files themselves -------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
